{"id":"0ec9a372-ef70-49c3-8b94-8fced99788cf","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"b9219c6246c4e360","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/margin/coverage.ts","baseline":{"blob":"8536e24f6686afb169a6a07ffac502156f923ff8","start":1462,"end":1537},"shape":{"type":"TypeAliasDeclaration","atoms":["type","Reports","=","Map","<","string",",","{","\"","report","\"",":","CoverageEvent",";","\"","anchors","\"",":","Anchors","}",">"]},"context":{"before":"005bf7e3dee34fdc","after":"858916f758d81a5c"}},"payload":{"text":"A file's latest report from each program that ran it, with its text to find statements from.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:45:54.492Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:45:54.492Z"}
{"id":"1a7b0067-8b08-4165-9722-f96cfbe3dd40","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"1e20df20625de121","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/margin/coverage.ts","baseline":{"blob":"1d276939b24218d0f25ed785862087839b23b859","start":0,"end":63},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","CoverageEvent","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/editor-api","\""]},"context":{"after":"0b86648dc9c14834"}},"payload":{"text":"Coverage, with nothing to ask for: every run a debugger reports on (its `coverage` event, as it ends) leaves its files marked,\nin the Margin's gutter column, just left of the code (a pane view of its own into the Margin): a mark beside each line that ran\nand beside each that didn't, saying how often, and the same colors in the scrollbar. Not in the glyph margin: VS Code won't set\na breakpoint where another extension's icon is, so that stays the breakpoints'.\n\nEach program's latest run of a file counts, so a line didn't run only if no run of any program reached it, and a test\nsuite's coverage adds up. Each statement is found again in the text as it is now (anchors.ts, its BABLR span), so a mark\nfollows its code through edits and a reformat; one edited past recognizing loses its mark until it runs again.\n\nRuns this session only: kept across a reload, they'd need the statements that didn't run, which the run record doesn't hold.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:45:59.255Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:45:59.255Z"}
{"id":"1f808df0-0da1-4c2b-acd2-8e68824920d1","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"21d58f64391f7563","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/margin/coverage.ts","baseline":{"blob":"83991164f3042c5209420ec63a256556432ec59c","start":2267,"end":2414},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","ran","=","vscode",".","window",".","createTextEditorDecorationType","(","{","\"","overviewRulerColor","\"",":","\"","#2ea04340","\"",",","\"","overviewRulerLane","\"",":","vscode",".","OverviewRulerLane",".","Left","}",")"]},"context":{"before":"9e92e4af3727b748#0","after":"14a02a6ecf92b03e"}},"payload":{"text":"(the scrollbar's: a decoration with no gutter icon, so breakpoints can still be set on the line)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:45:50.994Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:45:50.994Z"}
